.TH SYNADM-TUI-THUERINGEN 1 "September 2026" "synadm-tui 0.22" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
synadm-tui-thueringen \- Thüringen edition of synadm-tui
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B synadm-tui-thueringen
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B synadm-tui-thueringen
starts the Thüringen-branded edition of
.BR synadm-tui .
It uses the same application core, command line options, demo mode and package
behavior as
.BR synadm-tui ,
but starts with the Thüringen visual profile.
.SH OPTIONS
The options are identical to
.BR synadm-tui (1):
.TP
.B \-\-synadm " " \fIPATH\fR
Use an alternative synadm executable.
.TP
.B \-\-config-file " " \fIPATH\fR
Pass an alternative synadm configuration file to synadm.
.TP
.B \-\-timeout " " \fISECONDS\fR
Set the timeout for each synadm call.
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Start with the local demo backend.
.TP
.B \-\-demo-state " " \fIPATH\fR
Use a custom JSON file for the local demo backend state.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the program version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show command line help and exit.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
See
.BR synadm-tui (1).
The runtime demo toggle
.B d
also works in the Thüringen edition and marks the header with
.BR "// D E M O" .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/synadm-tui/theme-thueringen
Theme setting for the Thüringen edition.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/synadm-tui/demo-server.json
Default local demo backend state.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR synadm-tui (1),
.BR synadm (1)
.SH AUTHOR
synadm-tui contributors
